WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:11.633
A digital signal does not know the whole curve: only its value at certain instants, the sampling instants. Each point is a sample.

2
00:00:12.052 --> 00:00:20.863
The instant of sample n is n divided by the sampling rate. At 8000 hertz, 125 microseconds pass between one sample and the next.

3
00:00:21.558 --> 00:00:29.861
How many samples fit in one cycle? The sampling rate divided by the signal frequency: 8000 over 500 is 16 samples.

4
00:00:30.566 --> 00:00:36.878
As the frequency rises, fewer samples fit in each cycle. At 2000 hertz only 4 samples per cycle remain.

5
00:00:37.577 --> 00:00:45.731
With two samples per cycle we reach the limit: the Nyquist frequency, half the sampling rate. We will study it in unit 5.
